# Data licence — read this before reusing anything in derived/

**This repository does not and cannot license the data it derives.**

## What the sources say

All seven sources say a version of the same sentence:

```
5x  MISO   "publishes these openly; no stated reuse restriction"
1x  NYISO  "publishes this openly; no stated reuse restriction"
1x  SPP    "publishes this openly on its operations portal; no stated reuse restriction"
```

"No stated reuse restriction" is exactly the thing that is not a licence. These
are regional transmission organisations — private non-profit corporations, not
federal agencies — so their output is not US government work and does not fall
into the public domain by default. Nothing here was granted; it was merely not
forbidden.

## Why not CC-BY-4.0

This file previously carried the verbatim CC-BY-4.0 text. Applying CC-BY-4.0
asserts that this repository holds rights it can grant onward. It does not.
**The absence of a stated restriction upstream is not a grant of rights** — it
is silence, and silence cannot be relicensed.

What this repository can say is narrower and true: the capture adds a retrieval
timestamp and a parse. Neither creates a new right over the underlying values.

